# `fluid::RouteOptions`

The quality step, Courant limit and cell count of `transport` and `heat`.

## Signature

```cpp
fluid::RouteOptions
```

## What It Does

Sets the resolution of the quality clock, shared by constituent, age and thermal routing. Each pipe is cut into `cells` cells of equal volume; the step is shortened until no cell passes more than `courant` of its content.

## Fields

| Field | Meaning | Default |
|---|---|---|
| `step` | The longest quality step, s. | 300 |
| `courant` | The largest fraction of a cell or a draining tank that passes in a step, in `(0, 1]`. | 0.9 |
| `flow_tolerance` | A flow magnitude treated as stagnant, m³/s. | 1e-12 |
| `cells` | Equal-volume cells per pipe. | 16 |

## Returns

A value; validated by `transport` and `heat`.

## Errors

A non-positive step, a Courant number outside `(0, 1]`, a negative flow tolerance and a non-positive cell count are rejected.

## Interpretation and Use

More cells give a sharper front. At a Courant number of one the front moves one whole cell a step and is carried exactly; below one the scheme diffuses it. The hydraulic `Schedule::step` also cuts the quality step, so keep it a multiple of the quality step to hold a Courant number of one.

